  "summary": "One typed index/generation/registry identity model defines all seven rendering handles. Stable version leases preserve replacements through CPU use and optional GPU fences; owner-thread publication/retirement and EngineContext teardown guards enforce the transitional lifetime boundary. Exhaustion never revives stale identities. Debug/Release CPU, type-rejection, failure, GL/root and eight application smoke checks pass.",
